Z||000000||speed racer||10-16-2001||10:26 PM||||Can I replace the clutch with out pulling the motor.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gerald||10-16-2001||11:01 PM||||Yes. I did it. It took me awhile thou. Ill try a brife summery.<P>disconect the shifter cables from the tranny<P>use a engine hoist to support the engine by the back support mount.<P>remove the shift assembley from the tranny<P>remove the tranny mounts only ( not the motor mounts)<P>remove the flywheel inspection cover<P>remove the 6 engine to tranny bolts<P>use a second engine hoist to hold the tranny<P>pull the tranny away from the block and towards the back of the car<P>this gave me enuf room to remove the clutch but it was a tight fit<P>Good luck <P>------------------<BR>87 coupe 5 spd||||reg||1
Z||000002||lowCG||10-17-2001||09:07 PM||||That's the prefered way to do it,for me anyhow.I usually wind up dropping the cradle,leaving the motor up in there,but I like the way just described.<BR>You'd have to disconnect the lower balljoints and pull the axles from the trans also,wouldn't you?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gerald||10-18-2001||01:07 PM||||Opps sorry, you do have to pull the axels. That should only add another 10 to 30 mins.<P>------------------<BR>87 coupe 5 spd||||reg||1
Z||000004||Gerald||10-18-2001||01:09 PM||||oops sorry missed that. Got to pull the axels to but that shouldnt add much time.||||reg||1
